Hey Jordan,

Fair question, and I owe you a straight answer. I changed the onboarding
flow because I watched eleven session recordings and nine of those people
never got past the import step. They were not confused by the product, they
were confused by my explanation of it. So I cut the explanation.

The new flow drops you straight into a sample workspace that already has
data in it. You can break it, you can delete it, nothing is precious. From
what I can tell so far, people get to their first real result in about four
minutes instead of twenty.

If this made things worse for your team specifically, tell me what you were
doing before and I will put a switch in. I would rather ship a toggle than
lose you over a redesign.

Thanks for pushing on this. Most people just leave quietly.

Founder

